What is sleep dentistry for?
If you or your partner wake feeling unrested, sleep dentistry could offer relief. Snoring and other night-time breathing concerns may be a sign of obstructive sleep apnoea. This is when the airway becomes blocked during sleep, causing repeated pauses in breathing. For some people, a fitted oral device can help by gently moving the jaw and tongue forward to keep the airway clear.

Get started
→SUPPORT FOR A BETTER NIGHT’S SLEEP
