Clinical Director
A/Prof Andrew Huhtanen
A/Prof Andrew Huhtanen
Clinic Director
BSc, OD, GCertClinEd

Originally from Toronto, Canada, Andrew graduated as a Doctor of Optometry from the University of Waterloo, after completing a Bachelor of Science (Honours) from Queen’s University. He holds a Graduate Certificate in Clinical Education from the University of Melbourne.

Andrew is an Associate Professor in the Department of Optometry and Vision Sciences at the University of Melbourne, and has a passion for advancing eye care through education, clinical practice, and research. He has a strong interest in clinical training, student assessment, interdisciplinary clinical education and evidence-based patient care.

Andrew has consulted at a wide range of practices across Canada and Australia. His clinical areas of interest are in anterior eye disease and specialty contact lenses, including corneals, sclerals, hybrids, and orthokeratology, and managing complex conditions such as paediatric aphakia, keratoconus and corneal grafts.

Andrew has volunteered and lectured internationally in Mexico, India, Tanzania, Myanmar, and Thailand. Melbourne is now home, where he enjoys exploring Victora, running with his dog George, and cheering on the Richmond Tigers!

